cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."

title: "SnowClear: real-time, training-free snow-point detection and removal for LiDAR point clouds"

abstract: >-
  SnowClear detects and removes snowfall-induced noise from mechanical spinning
  LiDAR point clouds per point, at frame rate, on CPU, without training, GPU or
  learned weights. The algorithm core is ROS-agnostic and ships as a library
  with an offline CLI; a separate ROS 2 package wraps it as a point-cloud
  node. Both paths produce bit-identical detections, which is enforced by a
  byte-exact regression against a released reference output.

